sation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Verano Holdings Corp. is a micro-cap healthcare business with a $297M market cap on $822M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -9% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 50% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $12M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 18.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -2.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 9.8% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 13% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Healthcare peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 72% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 74% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Wall Street Analysts See a 285.48% Upside in Verano Holdings Corp. (VRNO): Can the Stock Really Move This High?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3023020/wall-street-analysts-see-a-285-48-upside-in-verano-holdings-corp-vrno-can-the-stock-really-move-this-high?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cconsensus_price_target-3023020","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793800503.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Verano Holdings Corp. (VRNO) Reports Q3 Loss, Lags Revenue Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3018645/verano-holdings-corp-vrno-reports-q3-loss-lags-revenue-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%